# The rehearsal's settings, never a secret. The kit's rehearsal (.open-autonomy/rehearsal/lib.ts) reads this file first
# and takes each line as a default; a variable exported in the shell wins. $HOME expands. Every line is optional.
#
# REHEARSAL_WORLD=__PROJECT__-rehearsal      the world's name (default: <owner>-<repo>-rehearsal)
# WORLD_STATE_ROOT=$HOME/.local/state/__PROJECT__   where the world keeps its state (default: this checkout);
#                                            the runtime admits a world against the free space of the root it is given
# TWINS_ROOT=$HOME/src/twin                  a twins checkout, when developing the twins (default: the published packages)
# OPEN_AUTONOMY_ROOT=$HOME/src/open-autonomy a backend checkout for the backend copy (default: @open-autonomy/backend)
# WORLD_HERMES_BIN=/opt/hermes/.venv/bin     a Hermes to run instead of installing the pin under the world's state
# REHEARSAL_VALVE_PORT=18887                 the brain's valve in the world (default 18887)
# REHEARSAL_PORT_OFFSET=100                  moves every port in world.json, for two worlds on one machine
#
# The stories speak of a client's repository and tracker; a project whose brain works someone else's names them:
# REHEARSAL_CLIENT_REPO=owner/repo           (default: this project's account)
# REHEARSAL_BRANCH_PREFIX=agent              the branch a pull request for KEY is opened on: <prefix>/KEY
# REHEARSAL_JIRA_PROJECT=PROJ  REHEARSAL_ASSIGNEE=twin:agent  REHEARSAL_CLIENT=client@example.test
